ENTRY 11463 {"id":11463,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"docs/session-api.md:31:| `POST /sessions` body `{ provider?, model?, repo?, branch? }` | `201 { sessionId, provider, model, reasoning? }` | Creates the session for the caller (the token's owner). No conversation or sandbox yet. The body is optional; without it the session runs the default model. `provider` and `model` go together and must be a pair on the allowlist (see Models), else `400 { \"error\": \"model <provider>/<model> is not allowed\" }`. `repo` (`owner/name` on github.com) and `branch` (optional) give the session a cloned repository workspace, see `docs/repo-workspace.md`; a bad value is `400` and `branch` without `repo` is `400`. The response echoes the model the session will use (and `repo`/`branch`), and the reasoning effort (`reasoning`, from `PI_MODEL_REASONING`; absent when unset). |\ndocs/research/onecli-spike.md:57:- Caveats: **existing data is owned by user `local-admin`** (agents, secrets) and will not be visible to the new Google user (re-create, or update `users.external_auth_id`). NextAuth has no email allowlist, so any Google account can sign in and gets its own project; restrict at the Google consent screen or put auth at the HTTPRoute. Gateway tokens keep working. The gateway port 10255 is cluster-only (the HTTPRoute exposes 10254 only).\ndocs/model-credentials.md:85:5. **Choose models** in ConfigMap `pi-model-config`, then restart ingest and the orchestrator (env is read at start):\ndocs/model-credentials.md:102:allowlist (400 otherwise) and stores it in `inbox.sessions`. The orchestrator creates the Pi conversation with that\ndocs/model-credentials.md:114:  allowlist stops new sessions only: existing conversations keep it.\npackages/ingest/src/config.ts:13:  /** Default model and allowlist for POST /sessions (same variables as the orchestrator, from one ConfigMap). */\npackages/orchestrator/test/host-model.test.ts:58:  it(\"keeps the model across a restart: a reopened Harness runs the conversation on it unchanged\", async () => {\npackages/orchestrator/test/host-model.test.ts:76:  it(\"stores the reasoning effort with the model, and keeps it across a restart\", async () => {\npackages/orchestrator/src/host.ts:137:  /** A further input to an existing session; the model follows the newest script. False if unknown. */\npackages/orchestrator/src/providers.ts:22: * allowlist's providers, the scripted ones, and `faux` for the Phase 3 /control sessions.\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:276:   * Turns are model responses, counted from the stored transcript, so a restart does not reset the count.\n    65\t/** The Pi Durable host: one Harness over the Postgres storage, one conversation per session. */\n    66\texport class Host {\n    67\t  readonly #harness: Harness;\n    68\t  readonly #sandboxes: Sandboxes;\n    69\t  readonly #storage: Storage;\n    70\t\n    71\t  private constructor(harness: Harness, sandboxes: Sandboxes, storage: Storage) {\n    72\t    this.#harness = harness;\n    73\t    this.#sandboxes = sandboxes;\n    74\t    this.#storage = storage;\n    75\t  }\n    76\t\n    77\t  /**\n    78\t   * Opens the Harness over an owned storage and resumes whatever the last process left running.\n    79\t   * `onFailed` fires when the Harness ends on a storage error, e.g. the database connection died.\n    80\t   */\n    81\t  static async open(\n    82\t    storage: Storage,\n    83\t    config: OrchestratorConfig,\n    84\t    onFailed: (error: unknown) => void,\n    85\t    sessionKeyOf: SessionKeyOf,\n    86\t    hooks: SandboxHooks = {},\n    87\t    recycleAtStart: readonly number[] = [],\n    88\t  ): Promise<Host> {\n    89\t    const models = await buildModels(config);\n    90\t    const registry = createRegistry();\n    91\t    registry.install(createCodingTools());\n    92\t    const sandboxes = new Sandboxes(config, sessionKeyOf, hooks);\n    93\t    // Before resume(): a continuing run must not run its next command in a Pod that still holds the leftovers of\n    94\t    // the command the previous process was killed in.\n    95\t    sandboxes.recycleAtStart(recycleAtStart);\n    96\t\n    97\t    const harness = await Harness.open(\n    98\t      storage,\n    99\t      {\n   100\t        models,\n   101\t        registry,\n   102\t        // Lazy: the SandboxClaim is created at the first tool call, not at the first model request.\n   103\t        env: ({ conversationId }) => Promise.resolve(sandboxes.lazyEnv(Number(conversationId))),\n   104\t        onReport: (report) => {\n   105\t          log(\"report\", { kind: report.kind, message: errorMessage(report.error) });\n   106\t        },\n   107\t      },\n   108\t      context,\n   109\t    );\n   110\t    void harness.closed.then((end) => {\n   111\t      if (end.kind === \"failed\") onFailed(end.error);\n   112\t    });\n   113\t    // No new input needed: open recovers nothing by itself, resume() continues unfinished runs.\n   114\t    harness.resume();\n   115\t    return new Host(harness, sandboxes, storage);\npackages/orchestrator/test/providers.test.ts:54:    expect(models.getModel(\"scripted\", \"scripted-1\")).toBeDefined();\npackages/orchestrator/test/providers.test.ts:55:    expect(models.getModel(\"scripted\", \"scripted-2\")).toBeDefined();\npackages/orchestrator/test/providers.test.ts:56:    expect(models.getModel(\"faux\", \"faux-1\")).toBeDefined();\npackages/orchestrator/test/providers.test.ts:57:    expect(models.getModel(\"openrouter\", \"openai/gpt-4.1-nano\")).toBeUndefined();\npackages/orchestrator/test/providers.test.ts:67:    const model = models.getModel(\"openrouter\", \"openai/gpt-4.1-nano\");\npackages/orchestrator/test/providers.test.ts:98:    const model = models.getModel(\"openai-codex\", \"gpt-6.1-terra\");\npackages/orchestrator/src/providers.ts:69:    if (models.getModel(choice.provider, choice.model) === undefined) {\n    17\t/**\n    18\t * The `Models` of the orchestrator.\n    19\t *\n    20\t * Pi Durable stores a conversation's model as `{ provider, modelId }` names and resolves them against this `Models`\n    21\t * at every request, so every provider a stored conversation may name must be installed at every start: the\n    22\t * allowlist's providers, the scripted ones, and `faux` for the Phase 3 /control sessions.\n    23\t *\n    24\t * Real providers resolve their API key to a placeholder (`placeholderAuthContext`) and send their requests through\n    25\t * the OneCLI gateway, which replaces the placeholder with the credential it holds. Throws when an allowlisted model\n    26\t * is not in pi-ai's catalog, so a typo in the ConfigMap fails at start instead of at the first request.\n    27\t */\n    28\texport async function buildModels(\n    29\t  config: OrchestratorConfig,\n    30\t  readCa: (path: string) => Promise<string> = (path) => readFile(path, \"utf8\"),\n    31\t): Promise<Models> {\n    32\t  const models = createModels({\n    33\t    authContext: placeholderAuthContext,\n    34\t    credentials: await placeholderCredentials(config.onecli.codexAccountId),\n    35\t  });\n    36\t  models.setProvider(scriptedProvider({ provider: \"faux\" }).provider);\n    37\t  models.setProvider(\n    38\t    scriptedProvider({\n    39\t      provider: \"scripted\",\n    40\t      models: [{ id: \"scripted-1\" }, { id: \"scripted-2\" }],\n    41\t    }).provider,\n    42\t  );\n    43\t\n    44\t  const remote = config.models.allowed.filter((choice) => !LOCAL.has(choice.provider));\n    45\t  const token = config.onecli.token;\n    46\t  if (remote.length === 0 || token === undefined) {\n    47\t    assertInstalled(models, config);\n    48\t    return models;\n    49\t  }\n    50\t  const wanted = new Set(remote.map((choice) => choice.provider));\n    51\t  for (const provider of builtinProviders()) {\n    52\t    if (wanted.has(provider.id)) models.setProvider(provider);\n    53\t  }\n    54\t  assertInstalled(models, config);\n    55\t  const ca = await readCa(config.onecli.caFile);\n    56\t  return withFetch(\n    57\t    models,\n    58\t    createGatewayFetch({\n    59\t      gateway: config.onecli.gateway,\n    60\t      token,\n    61\t      ca,\n    62\t      noProxy: config.onecli.noProxy,\n    63\t    }),\n    64\t  );\n","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 11497 {"id":11497,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"## Findings\n### 1. Removing a provider from the allowlist breaks existing conversations\n- Severity: high\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/orchestrator/src/providers.ts:44\n- What happens: If the last model for a remote provider is removed from the allowlist and the orchestrator restarts, that provider is not installed. Existing conversations using it can no longer resolve their stored model for subsequent requests or resumed runs. The documented policy says allowlist removal stops new sessions only.\n- Evidence: `const wanted = new Set(remote.map((choice) => choice.provider));` followed by `if (wanted.has(provider.id)) models.setProvider(provider);`\n- Fix idea: Install providers needed by persisted conversations independently of the new-session allowlist, and configure the gateway whenever those conversations require it. Add a restart test that removes a provider from the allowlist while retaining a conversation that uses it.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
